//
// Inter-service gRPC contract for the configurable per-source companion-EXP
// rules layer (Identity supporting domain, chora_identity database). The
// resolver runs the precedence ladder (tenant override → platform plan →
// exp_source_def catalogue default) server-side; callers receive the winning
// rule for one occurrence of a verified EXP source.
//
// Primary caller:
//   - chora-consumption — companion growth award path (ADR-218 D6: the live
//     in-code growth/curve.go map is unified onto this resolver; the in-code
//     map remains ONLY as the documented fail-loud-logged fallback when this
//     service is unreachable — parity seeds guarantee identical values).
//
// INVARIANT (ADR-203 L16 — verified-EXP anti-gaming): the EXP source is
// ALWAYS a Chora-verified system event and is NON-CONFIGURABLE. This RPC
// tunes value / cap / eligibility / enabled of KNOWN sources only; an
// unknown source_code returns INVALID_ARGUMENT — it can NEVER mint a new
// source.
//
// Read-only + side-effect free: no idempotency key needed. Callers MAY
// cache responses briefly (rules change via rare H+ editor actions).
//
// Deployed in chora-local team-platform pool. mTLS via the service mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
// =============================================================================

